Feature: PySpark conversion and validation for Supplier Invoice Oracle Financials ETL

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks" and schema is "purgo_playground"
    And all required tables are available in the catalog
    And all referenced functions from ReusableFunctions and Constants are imported and available in PySpark
    And input parameters are provided via widgets:
      | name                   | type    | example value           |
      | target_table_path      | string  | "/mnt/purgo/target"     |
      | partition              | string  | "fscl_yr_nbr"           |
      | table_format           | string  | "delta"                 |
      | compression            | string  | "snappy"                |
      | table_name             | string  | "fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin" |
      | unity_catalog          | string  | "purgo_databricks"      |
      | environment            | string  | "prod"                  |
      | project                | string  | "ccg_rsd_eu"            |
      | load_type              | string  | "full"                  |
      | view_unity_catalog_name| string  | "vw_supplier_invoice"   |
      | raw_unity_catalog      | string  | "purgo_raw"             |
      | raw_unity_catalog_hist | string  | "purgo_raw_hist"        |
      | config_unity_catalog   | string  | "purgo_config"          |
      | edp_lkp_unity_catalog  | string  | "purgo_edp_lkp"         |
      | dims_unity_catalog     | string  | "purgo_dims"            |

  Scenario Outline: Successful PySpark ETL for supplier invoice fact table
    Given all required input tables are loaded as DataFrames
    And the control table is read successfully
    When the PySpark pipeline applies the business logic as per the SQL transformation
    And all joins, filters, and field mappings are performed as specified
    And all hardcoded and NULL fields are set as per requirements
    And the output DataFrame is written to <target_table_path> in <table_format> format with <compression> compression
    And the table is partitioned by <partition>
    Then the output table "<table_name>" in Unity Catalog "<unity_catalog>" contains the expected transformed data

    Examples:
      | target_table_path      | table_format | compression | partition      | table_name                          | unity_catalog      |
      | /mnt/purgo/target      | delta        | snappy      | fscl_yr_nbr    | fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin     | purgo_databricks   |
      | /mnt/purgo/target2     | parquet      | gzip        | invc_entry_dt  | fact_wf_supplier_invoice_orafin     | purgo_databricks   |

  Scenario Outline: Validation of required fields and types
    Given the input DataFrame contains the following field "<field>"
    When the pipeline validates the field type is "<type>"
    Then the field "<field>" is present and of type "<type>"
    And if the field is required and missing, an error "Missing required field: <field>" is raised

    Examples:
      | field                  | type    |
      | invoice_id             | string  |
      | invoice_accounting_date| date    |
      | transaction_amount     | double  |
      | supplier_party_id      | string  |
      | supplier_site_id       | string  |
      | invoice_number         | string  |

  Scenario Outline: Validation of allowed values for specific fields
    Given the field "<field>" in the input DataFrame
    When the value is not in allowed values <allowed_values>
    Then an error "Invalid value for <field>: <value>" is raised

    Examples:
      | field                  | allowed_values         |
      | invoice_source_code    | ['Receivables', 'MAINFRAME', 'OTHER'] |
      | gl_balancing_segment   | [400, 700, 900]       |

  Scenario: Filter out excluded supplier numbers
    Given the supplier_number is in [00032238, 00032239, 00080463, 90000147]
    When the pipeline processes the data
    Then the record is excluded from the output

  Scenario: Filter out excluded GL code combinations
    Given the concat_segments field after removing '.' is in the exclusion list
    When the pipeline processes the data
    Then the record is excluded from the output

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing input tables
    Given the input table "<table>" is missing or not loaded
    When the pipeline attempts to join or reference "<table>"
    Then an error "Input table not found: <table>" is raised

    Examples:
      | table                        |
      | dw_ap_sla_aging_invoice_ca   |
      | dw_ap_sla_expense_dist_cf    |
      | dw_party_d                   |
      | dw_supplier_site_d           |
      | dw_internal_org_d_tl         |
      | dw_ap_terms_d_tl             |
      | dw_natural_account_d         |
      | dw_ap_sla_payments_cf        |
      | dw_gl_segment_d_tl           |
      | dw_gl_code_combination_d     |
      | edp_lkup                     |
      | dim_wf_company               |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for missing function definitions
    Given the function "<function>" is referenced in the pipeline
    When the function is not defined or imported
    Then an error "Function not found: <function>" is raised

    Examples:
      | function                |
      | get_basejob_url         |
      | read_control_table      |

  Scenario Outline: Error handling for type mismatches
    Given the field "<field>" is expected to be of type "<expected_type>"
    When the actual type is "<actual_type>"
    Then an error "Type mismatch for <field>: expected <expected_type>, got <actual_type>" is raised

    Examples:
      | field                  | expected_type | actual_type |
      | transaction_amount     | double        | string      |
      | invoice_accounting_date| date          | string      |
      | supplier_party_id      | string        | int         |

  Scenario: Duplicate record handling
    Given multiple records exist for the same invoice_id
    When the pipeline applies row_number partitioning and filtering
    Then only the latest snapshot_captured_date record is retained per invoice_id

  Scenario Outline: NULL and hardcoded field logic
    Given the field "<field>" is set to NULL or a hardcoded value "<value>"
    When the business logic requires a different mapping
    Then an error "Business logic missing for <field>" is raised
    And the field "<field>" must be mapped as per updated requirements

    Examples:
      | field              | value      |
      | document_type      | NULL       |
      | txn_ref_nbr        | NULL       |
      | spend_type_cd      | 'Indirect' |

  Scenario: Output DataFrame write validation
    Given the output DataFrame is ready
    When writing to the target path with specified format and compression
    Then the write operation completes successfully
    And the table is registered in Unity Catalog with correct schema and partitioning

  Scenario: Output DataFrame post-processing
    Given the output DataFrame is written
    When post-processing steps are required (e.g., table registration, view creation)
    Then all post-processing steps are completed as per requirements

# END